{"id": "unknown-2026-06-09-010", "date": "2026-06-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Brunei tenders solar at five government buildings", "content": "<p>A tender is open in Brunei for the development of grid-connected solar installations on the rooftop and carports of five government buildings. The deadline to submit applications is June 23.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/09/brunei-tenders-solar-at-five-government-buildings/\">Brunei tenders solar at five government buildings</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/09/brunei-tenders-solar-at-five-government-buildings/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-09-011", "date": "2026-06-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Baks launches ballast-based flat-roof mounting solution", "content": "<p>The Polish manufacturer said its new product is designed for fast, non-penetrative deployment. It combines corrosion-resistant materials and simplified assembly to support efficient, scalable rooftop solar installations in commercial and industrial projects.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/09/baks-launches-ballast-based-flat-roof-mounting-solution/\">Baks launches ballast-based flat-roof mounting solution</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/09/baks-launches-ballast-based-flat-roof-mounting-solution/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-09-012", "date": "2026-06-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -1.0, "keywords": ["loss"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Study finds ‘significant’ agrivoltaic potential in Austria", "content": "<p>A techno-economic study in Austria evaluates agrivoltaic systems using a spatial simulation framework that jointly models solar power generation and crop production under current and future climate conditions. Results show ground-mounted PV delivers the highest electricity output and profits, while agrivoltaics reduce agricultural losses but offer only modest climate adaptation benefits compared to PV-only systems.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/09/study-finds-si", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/09/study-finds-significant-agrivoltaic-potential-in-austria/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-09-013", "date": "2026-06-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 1.0, "keywords": ["record"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Global solar tracker market grew 19% in 2025", "content": "<p>Analysis by Wood Mackenzie finds global tracker shipments reached a record 134 GWdc last year, with US-based Nextpower maintaining the largest market share for the eleventh consecutive year.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/09/global-solar-tracker-market-grew-19-in-2025/\">Global solar tracker market grew 19% in 2025</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/09/global-solar-tracker-market-grew-19-in-2025/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-09-014", "date": "2026-06-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "InfinityPV releases solar simulator with 385–1,300 nm illumination spectral range", "content": "<p>The Danish company said its ISOSun Pro Solar Simulator has 20 independently tunable LED wavelengths. It delivers intensities of up to 7 suns. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/09/infinitypv-releases-solar-simulator-with-385-1300-nm-illumination-spectral-range/\">InfinityPV releases solar simulator with 385–1,300 nm illumination spectral range</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/09/infinitypv-releases-solar-simulator-with-385-1300-nm-illumination-spectral-range/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-09-015", "date": "2026-06-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "From ‘crazy vision’ to 698 GW: How a bold solar forecast became too conservative", "content": "<p>In 2012, our \"300 GW/a PV initiative\" set out a vision of a very ambitious annual global PV market by 2025. At the time, many dismissed the target as \"crazy.\" Instead, reality has gone far beyond that ambition: according to the latest figures from the IEA PVPS, the world installed 698 GW of new PV capacity in 2025, which is more than double our original vision.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/09/from-crazy-vision-to-698-gw-how-a-bold-solar-forecast-became-too-cons", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/09/from-crazy-vision-to-698-gw-how-a-bold-solar-forecast-became-too-conservative/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-09-016", "date": "2026-06-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "The different options for energy storage", "content": "<p>Energy storage is essential to ensuring grid stability as demand grows for intermittent renewables, like solar PV. Different options are gaining traction, supported by international standards.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/09/the-different-options-for-energy-storage/\">The different options for energy storage</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/09/the-different-options-for-energy-storage/", "type": "rss"}]}
